        "notes": "The class axiomatises traceMassDiff and counitForm as free real fields with no construction, then the 'conjecture' field `converges` simply asserts they are equal. Because traceMassDiff is an uninterpreted ℝ (not built from any tr_M tower), the conditional corollary qbeta_is_trace_mass_difference (lean:52-55) is provable by rw and asserts only 'an unconstrained real equals the counit form given that we postulated it equals it'. The genuine content (the tower sum actually equalling the counit form) is not encoded — traceMassDiff is not defined as 𝔪(n)-𝔪(p)-m_e in Lean, only named so in a docstring. Borderline self-assuming carrier: the conjectural field carries the conclusion as a bare equality of two opaque symbols rather than the structural identity."
