        "notes": "The justification 'the two sides are the same physical observable ... so their equality is required for consistency' is a self-referential argument: it presumes both functionals compute the same observable (the thing to be shown) to argue they must be equal. The +0.17% residual (md:32-34) is precisely a measured *disagreement*, yet it is reframed as 'the brane-tower remainder' rather than evidence against the identity. Assuming the conclusion (they are the same observable) to motivate the conjecture is circular reasoning, though it is labelled a conjecture not a proof."
